## Derived anatomical assets (`blender-hand/`, `web/public/assets/`)

The hand bone meshes are derived from:

- **BodyParts3D** — Database Center for Life Science (DBCLS), Japan  
  https://dbarchive.biosciencedbc.jp/en/bodyparts3d/  
  License: **Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 2.1 Japan (CC BY-SA 2.1 JP)**

- **Z-Anatomy** — https://www.z-anatomy.com/  
  License: **Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike (CC BY-SA)**

Derived meshes, the rigged Blender scene, glTF export, stills, and motion
render are therefore distributed under **CC BY-SA** (share-alike). If you
remix these assets, you must attribute BodyParts3D and Z-Anatomy and share
derivatives under a compatible CC BY-SA license.

### Required attribution

> Hand bone geometry derived from BodyParts3D (DBCLS) and Z-Anatomy,  
> licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike.

The HandRig armature, animation markers, scene-spec tooling, and web
application code are separate from the anatomical mesh copyright and are
MIT-licensed as above (except where they embed the CC BY-SA meshes).
